      "extract": "[]{#sec:intro label=\"sec:intro\"} Effective theories are a powerful framework to exploit a separation of scales in a physical system. The long-distance degrees of freedom must be included dynamically in the effective theory, while short-distance physics enters only through the values of a few coupling constants, often called low-energy constants. Effective theories are widely used in many areas of physics. Recently,",
      "extractCut": true
