      "extract": "[]{#sec:effT:3body label=\"sec:effT:3body\"} The low-energy properties of the three-body system for a given effective potential can be obtained by solving the Faddeev equations. The full wave function can be decomposed into four components: one for each two-body subcluster and one for the three-body cluster [@Meier:hj]. For identical bosons, the three-body wave function is fully symmetric under exchange of particles",
      "extractCut": true
