      "extract": "[]{#sec:effT:4body label=\"sec:effT:4body\"} We now turn to the four-body sector. The four-body binding energies are given by the Yakubovsky equations which are a generalization of the Faddeev equations to the four-body system. The full four-body wave function $\\Psi$ is first decomposed into Faddeev components, followed by a second decomposition into Yakubovsky components. For identical bosons, one has two Yakubovsky",
