      "extract": "The four-body spectrum is most conveniently discussed in a generalized Efimov plot. This plot was introduced by Vitaly Efimov to summarize the universal properties of the three-body spectrum [@Efimov71; @Braaten:2004rn]. The set of all possible low-energy three-body states can be represented as points $(a^{-1}, K)$ on the plane whose horizontal axis is $1/a$ and whose vertical axis is the momentum variable",
